WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
Think clearly in a technical interview. Make your reasoning visible by clarifying the problem, testing the solution, and discussing tradeoffs.

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:09.500
Step 1. Clarify the problem. Confirm inputs, outputs, constraints, and the behavior expected in edge cases.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.250
Step 2. State an approach. Describe a workable plan before writing details so the interviewer can follow your reasoning.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:19.000
Step 3. Test while you build. Use a normal case, a boundary case, and a failure case to catch assumptions early.

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.750
Step 4. Discuss tradeoffs. Compare complexity, maintainability, and performance instead of claiming one perfect answer.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:28.500
When stuck. Recover out loud. Summarize what you know, name the blocker, and choose the next small test.
